:{"accessibility":["Pins are focusable buttons in reading order (top-to-bottom, then left-to-right) with an accessible name such as \"Comment by meilin on Button #checkout-submit, ready for review, 3 messages\"; Enter opens the bubble and Escape closes it and returns focus to the pin.","The thread bubble is a labelled dialog; on phones it becomes a bottom sheet with the same controls and a visible close button.","Status is never conveyed by color alone: every status badge and pin state carries an icon and a word (open, ready for review, resolved).","Focus is a 2px Iris outline at 2px offset on every control, never removed and never covered by the sticky palette or tab bar.","Tablet and phone tiers use 44px touch targets for tools, chips and pins; keyboard shortcut hints are hidden there.","No text renders below 12px in any Locale; controls use 13px and prose 14px, and zh-TW line heights grow by about 2px.","Light and dark themes meet WCAG 2.2 AA: text 4.5:1, pins, control boundaries and focus rings 3:1, as verified in DESIGN.md."],"constraints":["The Workbench is a projection over shared application semantics and never writes canonical files directly; comments, replies and lifecycle changes go through the Review authoring operations.","The iframe stays at its canonical logical viewport size and only the outer frame scales; pins, bubbles and blueprint labels live in the Workbench overlay, never inside the iframe, and no transparent pointer-capture layer covers the iframe.","Primary navigation stays in the Rail (and the TabBar on phones); the 48px top bar holds only the Workspace switcher, breadcrumb, search and the member menu, honoring Decision 47eb4ce7 to keep RootShell free of a top navigation bar.","The Canvas First Rule: at FHD the canvas keeps at least 60% of the viewport width with both side panels open.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md: graphite chrome, Iris violet only for selection, focus and the single primary action per region, Marker magenta only for human annotation, and status hues only in badges, icons and alerts.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets; zh-TW uses Taiwan Traditional Chinese with full-width punctuation and keeps domain nouns (View, Variant, Widget, Workspace, Review, Spec, UX Flow, Handoff, Adapter, Locale, Asset, Decision, Owner, Checks, Evidence) in English.","Identities and measurements stay literal and use the mono blueprint register: Widget ids such as #checkout-submit, Widget type names, revisions, keyboard keys and CLI commands are never translated."],"decisions":[{"history":[{"actor":{"displayName":"Reviewer","type":"human"},"after":{"outcome":{"rationale":"Avoid cluttered layout in initial dogfooding wave.","summary":"Decision made to keep RootShell minimal without top navigation."},"status":"decided"},"at":"2026-10-04T06:36:53.174Z","before":{"status":"pending"},"source":{"reviewId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321"}}],"id":"47eb4ce7-4359-480c-ac56-82473696776c","outcome":{"rationale":"Avoid cluttered layout in initial dogfooding wave.","summary":"Decision made to keep RootShell minimal without top navigation."},"provenance":{"reviewId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321","sourceReviewThreadId":"140f4e87-cc50-4768-a82b-56b663609321"},"question":"Should we add top navigation bar to RootShell?","status":"decided"}],"entryConditions":["A signed-in member opened a View from Views, from a Reviews thread (\"Open in canvas\"), or from a deep link that names a View and optionally a Variant and a thread.","The Workspace Adapter set resolved and the preview session is live; otherwise the preview-error Variant applies.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset (desktop 1920 × 1080, tablet 1024 × 768, or mobile 390 × 844), one Locale (en-US default or zh-TW), and one theme (light or dark). All twelve combinations are authored and captured explicitly."],"intent":"Let a reviewer judge a running View on the Quiet Canvas: the View sits in a lifted frame on a recessed canvas, human annotations float above it as teardrop pins, and a click opens the thread bubble where the reviewer reads, replies and resolves — without the tool competing with the thing being judged.","interactionRules":["The canvas tool palette floats centered at the bottom: Select (V), Comment (C) and Interact (I), then the pin visibility toggle (Shift+C). Exactly one tool is active; Select is the default.","Choosing Comment enters comment mode: the Comment tool tints Marker, a 2px Marker inset line runs along the top edge of the canvas, and a hint explains \"Click a Widget, or press Esc to cancel.\" (comment-mode Variant).","Pins are drawn only on Widgets that the iframe itself resolved; the pin tip marks the anchor point exactly, and positions follow live geometry per animation frame without tweening.","Clicking a pin opens its thread bubble anchored at the pin tip, preferring the right side and flipping to stay inside the canvas; the open pin gets a 2px Iris ring and its row in the Comments panel is selected (thread-open Variant).","The bubble shows the thread title, status badge, Variant scope, a mono target chip (\"Button · #checkout-submit\"), a compact timeline of messages and lifecycle events, a reply field, and lifecycle actions.","Resolving is a human-only Workbench action. On a ready-for-review thread the primary action reads \"Accept and resolve\" and accepts the named submission as Verified; on an open thread it reads \"Resolve\" and resolves as Answered, with other resolutions in its menu; afterwards the pin turns into a resolved graphite check, the bubble closes and a toast confirms it (thread-resolved Variant).","Comments whose anchor cannot be placed are never drawn at a guessed position; they are listed in the bottom-left tray and in the panel group \"Can't be placed\".","The right panel (desktop) lists Comments, Inspect, Spec and Readiness; Comments group threads into Ready for review, Open and Can't be placed, filterable by status.","When the View has no Widgets yet, the frame shows a dashed empty state that points to update_view_structure and offers \"Open the Spec\" (empty-view Variant).","When the Adapter set cannot load, the frame is replaced by a fault alert naming adapter.unresolved and the module path, with \"Copy repair command\" and \"Retry\"; the Widget tree and Spec stay available (preview-error Variant).","The context bar reports the live render context (Variant, Locale, Viewport, Theme) and changes only the previewed View, never the Workbench chrome theme or language.","Layout derives from the viewport width only: 1280px and wider shows the 264px Rail, the main region and (where present) a 340px right panel; 640–1279px collapses the Rail to a 56px icon rail and moves the right panel to on-demand; below 640px the Rail is replaced by the 56px bottom TabBar. On phones the View page switches between Spec, Comments and View tabs, and the thread bubble docks to a bottom sheet."],"references":[{"label":"Multi-target geometry tracking for comment pins","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/2#discussioncomment-18757811"},{"label":"Transport-level wire batching and the tablet pin budget","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/2#discussioncomment-18767954"},{"label":"Review pin display hint","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/7#discussioncomment-18757814"},{"label":"targeting.select click point","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/3#discussioncomment-18761696"},{"label":"Axis-aligned quad proof and the targeting wire","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/3#discussioncomment-18760674"},{"label":"Direct resolve of discussion threads (human-only, Workbench-only)","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/7#discussioncomment-18757815"},{"label":"Widget Event reporting for the Prototype player","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/2#discussioncomment-18760678"},{"relation":"thread-list","type":"view","viewId":"468247e8-4f39-4f04-8056-b2af4c1c37ea"},{"relation":"readiness","type":"view","viewId":"2e2f88d6-7a95-424a-b3d4-4661d811ef13"}]},"variants":{"comment-mode":{"state":{"canvas":{"mode":"comment"},"tool-comment":{"selected":true},"tool-select":{"selected":false}}},"empty-view":{"state":{"pins-layer":{"visible":false},"view-checkout":{"visible":false},"view-empty":{"visible":true}}},"preview-error":{"state":{"pins-layer":{"visible":false},"view-checkout":{"visible":false},"view-error-wrap":{"visible":true}}},"thread-open":{"state":{"pin-ml":{"selected":true},"row-ml":{"selected":true},"thread-bubble":{"open":true}}},"thread-resolved":{"state":{"pin-ml":{"status":"resolved"},"row-ml":{"status":"resolved"},"thread-bubble":{"open":false,"status":"resolved"},"toast-resolved":{"visible":true}}}}},"type":"view"},{"identity":{"id":"ebe9f7ea-0414-448d-8ddb-aea69a9e1cdd"},"revision":"r_KYQ0AiDPOidRtGLhc1kTp4g-THUlECi2Sadl8yOn4Ag","snapshot":{"feature":"access","id":"ebe9f7ea-0414-448d-8ddb-aea69a9e1cdd","ir":{"id":"root","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"align":"center","direction":"vertical","fillViewport":true,"gap":0,"justify":"center","padding":24,"responsive":{"compact":{"justify":"start","padding":"48px 16px"}},"surface":"elevated"},"id":"signin-page","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"card":true,"direction":"vertical","gap":16,"maxWidth":"100%","padding":24,"width":"384px"},"id":"signin-card","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":4},"id":"signin-heading","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"level":1,"text":{"$i18n":"signin.title"},"variant":"title"},"id":"signin-title","type":"Text"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"signin.description"},"tone":"muted","variant":"ui"},"id":"signin-description","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"description":{"$i18n":"signin.signingIn"},"icon":"key-round","tone":"info","visible":false},"id":"signin-progress","type":"Alert"},{"config":{"error":{"$i18n":"signin.errors.invalid"},"help":{"$i18n":"signin.tokenHelp"},"label":{"$i18n":"signin.tokenLabel"},"mono":true,"placeholder":{"$i18n":"signin.tokenPlaceholder"}},"id":"signin-token","type":"TextInput"},{"config":{"fullWidth":true,"icon":"log-in","label":{"$i18n":"signin.submit"},"variant":"primary"},"id":"signin-submit","type":"Button"},{"config":{"spacing":0},"id":"signin-divider","type":"Divider"},{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":4},"id":"signin-recover","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"signin.recoverTitle"},"tone":"highlighted","variant":"label"},"id":"signin-recover-title","type":"Text"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"signin.recover"},"tone":"muted","variant":"label"},"id":"signin-recover-body","type":"Text"},{"config":{"text":"uiux invite create --workspace <dir> --member <nick>","tone":"default","variant":"mono"},"id":"signin-recover-command","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Sign-in","spec":{"accessibility":["The card title is the level-1 heading; the token field has a visible label, help text tied to it, and an error announced with role=\"alert\" when invalid.","The primary button is the only Iris element and is full width with a 44px target on touch tiers; the token input uses 16px text on phones.","The CLI command wraps rather than overflowing the 384px card on narrow screens.","No text renders below 12px in any Locale; controls use 13px and prose 14px, and zh-TW line heights grow by about 2px.","Light and dark themes meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast for text and controls."],"constraints":["Tokens are never echoed back, logged or stored in the Workspace; the page is part of the host-local access roster flow.","Workbench chrome (Rail, TabBar, top bar) is not shown before sign-in.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md: graphite chrome, Iris violet only for selection, focus and the single primary action per region, Marker magenta only for human annotation, and status hues only in badges, icons and alerts.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets; zh-TW uses Taiwan Traditional Chinese with full-width punctuation and keeps domain nouns (View, Variant, Widget, Workspace, Review, Spec, UX Flow, Handoff, Adapter, Locale, Asset, Decision, Owner, Checks, Evidence) in English.","Identities and measurements stay literal and use the mono blueprint register: Widget ids such as #checkout-submit, Widget type names, revisions, keyboard keys and CLI commands are never translated."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["An unauthenticated browser requested any Workbench page, or a session expired.","A sign-in link (#uiux_i_…) in the URL fragment is redeemed automatically and never shown; this page is the fallback when there is no link.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset (desktop 1920 × 1080, tablet 1024 × 768, or mobile 390 × 844), one Locale (en-US default or zh-TW), and one theme (light or dark). All twelve combinations are authored and captured explicitly."],"intent":"Let a person reach a Workspace with as little ceremony as the access model allows: open the single-use sign-in link, or paste a member token, and land where they were going.","interactionRules":["The card explains both ways in: open the link that uiux dev or the Owner gave you, or paste a member token.","Sign in validates the pasted token with the server; while it runs the button is disabled and \"Signing you in…\" is announced (signing-in Variant).","An invalid, expired or already-used credential keeps the pasted value, marks the field invalid and explains that sign-in links work once and expire after 24 hours (invalid-token Variant).","The \"No link?\" footer shows the literal uiux invite create command that mints a fresh single-use link on the host.","After success the Workbench returns to the page that required sign-in; agents never use this page and authenticate with Authorization: Bearer tokens instead."],"references":[{"label":"LAN/team access, authentication and reviewer identity","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/1#discussioncomment-18757820"},{"label":"Member identity, roles, tokens and agent edit leases","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/1#discussioncomment-18758344"},{"relation":"after-sign-in","type":"view","viewId":"2e2f88d6-7a95-424a-b3d4-4661d811ef13"}]},"variants":{"invalid-token":{"state":{"signin-token":{"invalid":true,"value":"uiux_t_expired_7f3d…"}}},"signing-in":{"state":{"signin-progress":{"visible":true},"signin-submit":{"disabled":true},"signin-token":{"value":"uiux_t_••••••••••••"}}}}},"type":"view"},{"identity":{"id":"workspace"},"revision":"r_Qg92ysPoCTLBiS3CTm_6N58TA2GfUhbdmKtR8WtVqek","snapshot":{"adapters":[{"moduleSpecifier":"./adapters/reference.ts"}],"i18n":{"defaultLocale":"en-US"},"schemaVersion":2,"themes":{"dark":{"label":"Dark"},"light":{"label":"Light"}},"viewports":{"desktop":{"dimensions":{"height":1080,"width":1920},"label":"FHD Desktop"},"mobile":{"dimensions":{"height":844,"width":390},"label":"Mobile"},"tablet":{"dimensions":{"height":768,"width":1024},"label":"Tablet"}}},"type":"workspace"}],"roots":[{"type":"workspace"}],"schemaVersion":1}
